# Calculator, Edit > Paste: "12:m3:p:r*2=" (MS, M+, MR by their paste codes), C, pasted again
# Port side: the text goes onto the clipboard with "clip"; the reference frames come from
# calc-paste1.scn (Program Manager shell, Notepad copies the text; its frames before
# Calculator pastes are not compared, only those of Calculator's window); recorded with
# dosbox-x_MinGWx64_SDL2.exe (its FPU computes with the host x87, as a real 387 would).
# regress: ARCH311_APP=apps/build/calc sh tools/run-cp-test.sh "$TEST" "$OUT"
# compare: calc-paste1/01.png 01.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste1/02.png 02.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste1/03.png 03.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste1/04.png 04.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# ini: WIN.INI SciCalc layout=
sleep 400
sleep 400
shot shots/01.png
clip 12:m3:p:r*2=
key alt
key e
key p
sleep 400
shot shots/02.png
key esc
sleep 400
shot shots/03.png
key alt
key e
key p
sleep 400
shot shots/04.png
